  _Case("Infective endocarditis","Cardiology","A 42-year-old has fever, malaise and new breathlessness with a newly detected murmur.","Recent dental infection and known bicuspid aortic valve.","Fever, splinter haemorrhages and a changing regurgitant murmur.","Multiple blood culture sets before antibiotics if this does not delay urgent treatment; echocardiography and inflammatory markers.","Fever, a predisposing valve lesion and new regurgitation suggest endocardial infection.","Rheumatic valve disease, non-bacterial thrombotic endocarditis, vasculitis and occult sepsis.","Urgent specialist assessment, obtain cultures, perform echo and tailor prolonged antimicrobial therapy to organism and susceptibility.","Why should blood cultures be collected before antibiotics in a stable suspected case?","To maximise microbiological yield and identify the causative organism","Prior antibiotics can sterilise blood cultures and make pathogen-directed treatment more difficult."),
